{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"7ae0421ecb8eb564b56af4ccf9a819d3c200c4bef6c8a022042377dbbd70675f","slug":"facet2.funding-intro","location":"/facet2/funding_intro.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Funding academic open source","short_title":"✅ Funding open source","content_includes_title":false,"numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"thumbnail":"/playbook/build/funding-cf912b4918891f4702241e3d87ba3521.svg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"funding_intro.md","url":"/playbook/build/funding_intro-1c6fccb578309537560e8e23a7d3276b.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/playbook/build/funding-cf912b4918891f4702241e3d87ba3521.svg","alt":"Stylized illustration of two people holding up a large dollar bill.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"kO7jSww3IF","urlSource":"../images/funding.svg"}],"class":"dark:hidden","key":"msPS1BwwUC"},{"type":"div","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/playbook/build/funding_darkmode-bde6f6807c2898ac8cb254b160ed8443.svg","alt":"Stylized illustration of two people holding up a large dollar bill.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"Fb1CMjaVCE","urlSource":"../images/funding_darkmode.svg"}],"class":"hidden dark:block","key":"SR41J7gWGS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Funding: it’s on everybody’s mind. It’s well-known that funding for open source is hard to come by, despite the critical importance of open source infrastructure (","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"Uuu6vmRiys"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.fordfoundation.org/learning/library/research-reports/roads-and-bridges-the-unseen-labor-behind-our-digital-infrastructure/","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eghbal, 2016","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"QPQfpqHQVy"}],"urlSource":"https://www.fordfoundation.org/learning/library/research-reports/roads-and-bridges-the-unseen-labor-behind-our-digital-infrastructure/","key":"VG8FDHvjWt"},{"type":"text","value":", ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"ArXr0fLfhT"},{"type":"cite","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MIC.2014.88","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Goble, 2014","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"sN2MGVfcyh"}],"kind":"narrative","label":"Goble_2014","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.1109/MIC.2014.88","enumerator":"1","key":"eVNx7wKxhp"},{"type":"text","value":"). More than half of open source maintainers are not paid for their work, and nearly half report that they would like to be paid (","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"llcT79qeGy"},{"type":"link","url":"https://www.sonarsource.com/open-source-maintainer-survey-2023.pdf","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tidelift, 2023","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"tXtO7dCjeR"}],"urlSource":"https://www.sonarsource.com/open-source-maintainer-survey-2023.pdf","key":"KGo7K0rjPJ"},{"type":"text","value":"). In a survey of developers of academic research software, the vast majority reported that their institution does not provide adequate resources to fund their work (","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"pkFIxWmb46"},{"type":"link","url":"https://peerj.com/articles/cs-963/","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Carver et al. 2022","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"tlDnihfcA0"}],"urlSource":"https://peerj.com/articles/cs-963/","key":"kre7BpKDqn"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"taXYXYcUIw"}],"key":"S64Ll11Yz8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s the good news: there may be funding opportunities you haven’t considered or just haven’t had the time to learn about. Open source tooling often has broad appeal and a low barrier to entry for the community, facilitating opportunities for industry partnerships, nuanced licensing models, institutional support, and other funding mechanisms besides grants. Open source projects lend themselves well to a diverse funding portfolio.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"Dr9gtZsOKh"}],"key":"aAvFuoIIPD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here are just a few of the resourcing mechanisms leveraged by the projects we interviewed:","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"cfq3H0jB29"}],"key":"qDIBQBJfzy"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grants","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"w0sQNcWKMB"}],"key":"Azi5JISMsZ"},{"type":"text","value":": Nearly all of the projects we interviewed had, at one time or another, received grant funding.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"oZs2gLOZpI"}],"key":"mUde3SmQcW"}],"key":"tFGfZB68ZI"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In-kind donations","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"zZPwRontlZ"}],"key":"QUVA60LDGx"},{"type":"text","value":": In-kind contributions from the university, industry, collaborators, and community volunteers were one of the most common forms of support among the projects we interviewed.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"Lgd93DRqcL"}],"key":"vuNXezTZkg"}],"key":"C3Orv1cFlt"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Company staff","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"EIodsBmJF5"}],"key":"W9cJmklAAL"},{"type":"text","value":": Two of the projects we interviewed were primarily maintained by a full-time employee at a tech company.","position":{"start":{"line":24,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"fkMCvOAH3c"}],"key":"vEAVly9dZV"}],"key":"Hy4AtD6SCm"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Government-mediated industry partnerships","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"E1MpdDRJ6b"}],"key":"o8wKIUkeRr"},{"type":"text","value":": Some federal programs specifically fund industry-academia collaborations, bound by grants or other agreements.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"w6mo4Yfnhi"}],"key":"RWE0AFIp82"}],"key":"RXP7PNT9nF"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Industry consortia","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"cVWQ3s872S"}],"key":"tqjS3l9v0v"},{"type":"text","value":": UC is home to a number of industry consortia, where companies pay a membership fee to support projects of interest to their field.","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"N7GXbnQNkj"}],"key":"GHEWFRwENp"}],"key":"ibW0JIpCfo"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entrepreneurship","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"PpajVEU2CQ"}],"key":"cNgPNcTFs0"},{"type":"text","value":": Of course, the open source project could form its own company, with varying degrees of separation between the company and the maintainers of the free codebase.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"Wh0lpN3RV3"}],"key":"IMgjhj7oOp"}],"key":"CyxcnSyOZ7"}],"key":"LfuG19xfO9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"These mechanisms are not mutually exclusive. Some projects we interviewed have made use of all of them. For simplicity, we present only four categories of resourcing in this chapter, largely based on how they are handled by the university. Each of the following chapters is an umbrella topic that covers many types of arrangements.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"DIQQDW65Rh"}],"key":"d4Q0pcP0Ul"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"UC can be your partner in establishing and managing all of your funding sources. Your department’s contracts and grants liaison, sponsored projects team, and TTO, among others, are here to help your projects succeed while also remaining compliant with university policies. ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"nVcKCTgd5u"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Importantly, you should never assume that you are free to accept funds directly from a sponsor.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"w1B1U9eDPi"}],"key":"BARyqEOn5n"},{"type":"text","value":" In most cases, the university must accept these funds on your behalf. So get to know your friendly support staff: they are here to help.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"co3v67fuZF"}],"key":"U4lxtAzuG6"}],"key":"QQQzeJv3ff"}],"key":"RyokLNeZCN"},"references":{"cite":{"order":["Goble_2014"],"data":{"Goble_2014":{"label":"Goble_2014","enumerator":"1","doi":"10.1109/mic.2014.88","html":"Goble, C. (2014). Better Software, Better Research. <i>IEEE Internet Computing</i>, <i>18</i>(5), 4–8. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1109/mic.2014.88\">10.1109/mic.2014.88</a>","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/mic.2014.88"}}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Licensing at UC","short_title":"✅ Licensing at UC","url":"/facet1/licensing","group":"Facet 1 - Discoverability"},"next":{"title":"Sponsored awards","short_title":"✅ Sponsored awards","url":"/facet2/sponsored-projects","group":"Facet 2 - Funding"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}